<main class="flex-1"><!--$--><section class="relative hero-bg stone-grain pt-16 pb-20 md:pt-24 md:pb-28 border-b border-border overflow-hidden"><div class="absolute inset-0 grid-glow opacity-60"></div><div class="relative mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 md:px-6 text-center"><div class="inline-block text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-gold mb-4">About</div><h1 class="font-display text-4xl md:text-6xl leading-[1.05] max-w-4xl mx-auto">About <span class="gradient-gold-text">Egyptian Granite</span></h1><p class="mt-5 text-base md:text-lg text-muted-foreground max-w-2xl mx-auto">The Global Source for Premium Egyptian Granite — direct from Egypt&#x27;s quarries to international architectural, commercial, and monumental projects.</p></div></section><section class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 md:px-6 py-16 md:py-24 "><div class="max-w-3xl"><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="text-xs text-muted-foreground"><ol class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5"><li class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><a href="<?php echo esc_url(home_url('/')); ?>" class="hover:text-gold">Home</a><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3 w-3" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6" /></svg></li><li class="flex items-center gap-1.5"><span class="text-foreground">About</span></li></ol></nav></div><div class="mt-8 grid lg:grid-cols-3 gap-12"><div class="lg:col-span-2 space-y-6 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed"><p class="text-lg text-foreground">Egyptian Granite by EG is a factory-direct supplier, exporter, and manufacturer of premium Egyptian granite — blocks, slabs, tiles, stairs, countertops, monuments, and cut-to-size — for architectural, commercial, and monumental projects worldwide.</p><p>Our material is quarried in Egypt&#x27;s historic granite regions: <strong>Aswan</strong> in Upper Egypt (Black Aswan, Red Aswan, Gandola), <strong>Halayeb</strong> on the Red Sea coast (New Halayeb, Halayeb, White and Bianco Halayeb), <strong>South Sinai</strong> around Saint Katherine (Rosa Katrina), and the <strong>Sharka, Forsan, and Eastern Desert</strong> belts (Grey Shirka, Karnak Grey, Red Forsan, Red Horus, Rosa El Nasr, Rosa Hody, Verdi Ghazal). Every variety is processed in modern Egyptian factories with strict quality control across cutting, polishing, inspection, and packing.</p><p>Egypt&#x27;s granite heritage stretches back more than four thousand years. The same Aswan quarries that supplied pharaonic obelisks, sarcophagi, and temple statuary continue to ship premium granite today. That continuity — geological, technical, and cultural — is what makes Egyptian granite a first-choice specification for architects working on heritage restoration, civic landmarks, and contemporary towers alike.</p><p>We work directly with international architects, contractors, importers, stone distributors, and project developers. Our role is to translate a project specification into a delivered container: recommending the right granite type and finish, producing to drawing, inspecting every shipment, packing for ISPM-15 export, loading the container, and issuing the full set of documents your destination customs requires.</p><p>As a B2B export specialist, Egyptian Granite by EG offers factory-direct pricing, FOB and CIF quotations from Egyptian ports (Alexandria, Port Said, Sokhna), mixed-container loading across granite types and finishes, secure ISPM-15 wooden packing, pre-shipment inspection (including third-party SGS / Bureau Veritas on request), and worldwide shipping to the Middle East, Europe, Africa, Asia, and the Americas.</p><p>To start a project, send your material, finish, sizes, quantity, and destination port via our <a href="<?php echo esc_url(home_url('/contact')); ?>" class="text-gold hover:underline">Request a Quote</a> form. Our export team replies within one business day.</p></div><asid